This folder is a **small standalone check** for **playing later**, not for building the port. It does not download anything and does not read game files.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The game **does not boot yet** for end users. Results are a **hardware estimate only**. For disk space, Python, LLVM, .NET and your game package, use **`Check-PC.bat`** in the [main port repository](https://github.com/ProjectLeonidaL/leonida).

## Status

| What | Meaning |
|---|---|
| **Green** `[OK]` | Looks fine for the run estimate |
| **Yellow** `[!!]` | Works, but slow or tight (e.g. few CPU threads) |
| **Red** `[XX]` | Likely too weak or unsupported |
| Deep GPU / translator flags | Optional: Python 3.12+ and `run_check.py` (`-Full`) |

## Quick start

**The easy way:**

1. Open this folder in the Leonida clone (or copy the whole `leonida-checker` folder).
2. Double-click **`Check-Run.bat`** — colored report in CMD (ASCII **LEONIDA LEGACY** banner, green / yellow / red).
3. UI languages: `Check-Run.bat -Lang de|ru|tr|en` (or `LEONIDA_LANG`).

If **`LeonidaRunCheck.exe`** exists beside the batch file, the batch runs the exe instead of PowerShell.

**Optional (developers, Python 3.12+):**

```powershell
python -I leonida-checker/run_check.py --lang de
```

**Full Vulkan probe** (same rules as the build’s `vk_subgroup_info`):

```powershell
Check-Run.bat -Full -Lang de
```

## What it checks

| Check | How |
|---|---|
| **OS** | Windows 10/11 x64 (`gta6rt`) |
| **CPU** | Model name, logical processors (8+ ideal, 4–7 warn) |
| **RAM** | Installed and free GiB (16 GiB reference: [docs/retail_boot_intel_host.md](../docs/retail_boot_intel_host.md)) |
| **GPU** | `vulkaninfo --summary` (many Windows installs already have it) |

No Python, no .NET, no LLVM, no game folder scan.

## Build the .exe

`LeonidaRunCheck.exe` is not in git (`*.exe` is ignored). Build once:

```text
Check-Run.bat build
```

That runs `build_exe.ps1` (downloads `ps2exe.ps1` on first build, embeds `i18n/en.json` and `de.json`). Then use **`Check-Run.bat`** as usual.

**Files in this folder:**

| File | Role |
|---|---|
| `Check-Run.bat` | Start check (or `build` for the exe) |
| `Check-Run.ps1` | Checker logic and colors |
| `build_exe.ps1` | Creates `LeonidaRunCheck.exe` |
| `run_check.py` | Optional full GPU check with Python |
| `i18n/*.json` | UI: **en**, **de**, **ru**, **tr** |

## GitHub description (copy for repo or release)

Use **English** in GitHub “About”; other languages for mirrors or docs.

**English:**  
Leonida Legacy run checker — estimates whether your Windows PC (CPU, RAM, Vulkan GPU) could realistically run the GTA VI Xbox→PC static-recompilation port when it is playable. No game data. UI: EN, DE, RU, TR.

**Deutsch:**  
Leonida Legacy Lauf-Check — schätzt, ob dein Windows-PC (CPU, RAM, Vulkan-GPU) den GTA-VI-Xbox→PC-Port (statische Rekompilierung) später realistisch starten kann. Keine Spieldaten. Sprachen: EN, DE, RU, TR.

**Русский:**  
Проверка запуска Leonida Legacy — оценивает, сможет ли ваш ПК (CPU, ОЗУ, Vulkan GPU) реалистично запустить порт GTA VI (Xbox→PC, статическая рекомпиляция), когда он будет готов. Без данных игры. Языки: EN, DE, RU, TR.

**Türkçe:**  
Leonida Legacy çalıştırma kontrolü — Windows PC’nizin (CPU, RAM, Vulkan GPU) GTA VI Xbox→PC statik yeniden derleme portunu oynanabilir olduğunda gerçekçi şekilde çalıştırıp çalıştıramayacağını tahmin eder. Oyun verisi yok. Diller: EN, DE, RU, TR.

## vs Check-PC

| | **Check-Run** (here) | **Check-PC** ([leonida](https://github.com/ProjectLeonidaL/leonida)) |
|---|---|---|
| Goal | Run the game later | Build the port now |
| Python, .NET, LLVM, disk | No | Yes |
| Game package | No | Yes |
| CPU / RAM / GPU | Yes | Build tools + GPU |